IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ks-types`

-- KiwiSaver Act 2006 — GOAL 1: MEMBERSHIP.
--
--   "Does the Act apply to the person; does automatic enrolment apply to
--    this employment; when may they opt out and when does an opt-out take
--    effect; may they opt in, and how; and the periods for allocation and
--    transfers."
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2006_40.txt — ss 6, 10-21,
-- 33-35, 42, 48, 51, 56, 57.

§ `Goal 1 — membership`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- Completed years of age on a date.
GIVEN born IS A DATE, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age of someone born` born `on` d MEANS
    IF   `add years` born (DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR born) AT MOST d
    THEN DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR born
    ELSE DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR born MINUS 1

-- s 6(1) "This Act applies to an employee or other natural person only if,
-- at the time when the person becomes subject to the automatic enrolment
-- rules or opts in, the person— (a) is, or normally is, living in New
-- Zealand, or is an employee of the State services ... serving outside New
-- Zealand ...; and (b) is a New Zealand citizen or is entitled, in terms of
-- the Immigration Act 2009, to be in New Zealand indefinitely."
@ref s 6(1)
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to` p IF
        p's `living in New Zealand, or a qualifying State servant abroad`
    AND p's `a citizen or entitled to be in New Zealand indefinitely`

§§ `Automatic enrolment (ss 10-15)`

-- s 12(1) "Employment is temporary ... if— (a) ... a casual agricultural
-- worker ...; or (b) ... a contract of service that is for a period of 28
-- continuous days or less; or (c) ... described in section 28(1)(a)(ii) of the
-- Holidays Act 2003." (2)(b) employment temporary under (b) ceases to be so
-- "on the 28th day after the employee started the employment".
@ref s 12
GIVEN d IS A DATE, e IS AN Employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment is temporary on` d `, employment` e IF
    CONSIDER e's `kind of employment`
    WHEN `ordinary employment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `casual agricultural work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a contract of service for 28 continuous days or less` THEN d LESS THAN `the day` 28 `days after` (e's `started on`)
    WHEN `intermittent or irregular work under s 28(1)(a)(ii) of the Holidays Act 2003` THEN TRUE

-- s 12(2) "(b) in the case of employment which was temporary under
-- subsection (1)(b), on the 28th day after the employee started the
-- employment" — the day it becomes new employment, from which s 16 counts
-- too (changed after the independent pass). A contract that ends before then
-- never becomes new employment.
@ref s 12(2)(b)
GIVEN e IS AN Employment
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the new employment starts for` e MEANS
    IF   e's `kind of employment` EQUALS `a contract of service for 28 continuous days or less`
    THEN `the day` 28 `days after` (e's `started on`)
    ELSE e's `started on`

-- s 10 "The automatic rules apply to an employee who— (a) starts new
-- employment with an employer that is not an exempt employer; and (b) is not
-- a secondee; and (c) when they start the new employment, is aged— (i) 18
-- years or more; and (ii) less than the New Zealand superannuation
-- qualification age." s 11 new employment excludes temporary employment and
-- the same payroll or business; s 14(1) the listed cases; s 14(2) "the
-- automatic enrolment rules do not apply if the employee is already a member
-- of a KiwiSaver scheme". FORK F1: for employment temporary under s 12(1)(b),
-- age is taken on the 28th day, when it becomes new employment (s 12(2)).
@ref ss 6, 10, 11, 12, 14
@export Whether the automatic enrolment rules apply to an employee's new employment under ss 10-14 of the KiwiSaver Act 2006 (NZ): the Act applies to the person (s 6); the employer is not exempt; the employee is not a secondee; the employment is new (not temporary, nor the same payroll or business, nor excluded by s 14(1)); the employee is not already a member; and on starting they are aged 18 or more but under the New Zealand superannuation qualification age. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A Person  @desc Date of birth, the superannuation qualification age, residence and status, and whether already a member
      e IS AN Employment  @desc When the employment started, its kind, whether the employer is exempt, whether a secondee, and the s 11 and s 14 exclusions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `automatic enrolment applies to` p `, employment` e IF
        `the Act applies to` p
    AND NOT e's `the employer is exempt`
    AND NOT e's `a secondee`
    AND NOT e's `same payroll, same business, or the end of a secondment`
    AND NOT e's `excluded by s 14(1)`
    AND NOT p's `already a member of a KiwiSaver scheme`
    AND NOT (    e's `kind of employment` EQUALS `casual agricultural work`
             OR  e's `kind of employment` EQUALS `intermittent or irregular work under s 28(1)(a)(ii) of the Holidays Act 2003`)
    AND (    NOT e's `kind of employment` EQUALS `a contract of service for 28 continuous days or less`
         OR  e's `the short contract continued to the 28th day`)
    AND age AT LEAST 18
    AND age LESS THAN p's `New Zealand superannuation qualification age`
    WHERE
        age MEANS `the age of someone born` (p's `date of birth`) `on` (`the day the new employment starts for` e)

§§ `Opting out (ss 16-21)`

-- s 16 "may opt out at any time in the period beginning on the 13th day after
-- the date on which the person started the new employment and ending on the
-- close of the 55th day after".
@ref s 16
GIVEN started IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day to opt out, employment started` started MEANS
    `the day` 13 `days after` started

@ref s 16
GIVEN started IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to opt out, employment started` started MEANS
    `the day` 55 `days after` started

-- s 17(4) "An opt-out takes effect on the later of— (a) the 13th day after the
-- date on which the person started the new employment ...; and (b) the date
-- on which the opt-out notice is— (i) accepted by the Commissioner ...; or
-- (ii) received by the employer". s 18(2) a late notice may be accepted if
-- received within "92 days after the date on which the Commissioner receives
-- the first contribution".
@ref ss 16, 17(4), 18
GIVEN started IS A DATE, given IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the opt-out takes effect, employment started` started `, notice accepted or received` given MEANS
    IF given GREATER THAN `the day` 13 `days after` started THEN given ELSE `the day` 13 `days after` started

@ref ss 16, 18
@export Whether an opt-out notice is in time under ss 16 and 18 of the KiwiSaver Act 2006 (NZ): given between the 13th and the 55th day after the new employment started; or, late, where s 18(1)(b) applies (no information pack within 7 days, no product disclosure statement, events beyond the employee's control, or a mistake) and it is received within 92 days after the Commissioner received the first contribution, and the Commissioner accepts it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN started IS A DATE  @desc The day the new employment started
      given IS A DATE  @desc The day the opt-out notice was given
      `late ground` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether a ground in s 18(1)(b) applies
      `first contribution` IS A MAYBE DATE  @desc The day the Commissioner received the first contribution, if any
      accepted IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the Commissioner accepts a late notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the opt-out is in time, employment started` started `, notice given` given `, s 18 ground:` `late ground` `, first contribution received` `first contribution` `, Commissioner accepts:` accepted IF
        (    given AT LEAST `the first day to opt out, employment started` started
         AND given AT MOST `the last day to opt out, employment started` started)
    OR  (    `late ground` AND accepted
         AND given GREATER THAN `the last day to opt out, employment started` started
         AND CONSIDER `first contribution`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST f THEN given AT MOST `the day` 92 `days after` f)

§§ `Opting in (ss 33-35)`

DECLARE `Who may contract to opt in` IS ONE OF
    `the person alone`
    `a guardian in the person's name`
    `the person jointly with a guardian`
    `the person alone, having no guardian`
    `an Oranga Tamariki guardian in the person's name`
    `may not opt in`

-- s 33 "A person may opt in at any time provided— (a) the person is not
-- already a member ...; and (b) the person is not subject to the automatic
-- enrolment rules." s 34: 18 or more, alone; s 35(2): under 16, a guardian in
-- the person's name; (3) 16 or 17 with a guardian, jointly; (4) 16 or 17
-- with no guardian, alone; (5) under 16 with an Oranga Tamariki guardian,
-- that guardian. s 35(3) covers "a guardian or an Oranga Tamariki guardian"
-- (changed after the independent pass).
@ref ss 33-35
GIVEN p IS A Person, d IS A DATE, `auto-enrolled` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a guardian` IS A BOOLEAN, `Oranga Tamariki guardian` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who may contract to opt in`
`who may opt in` p `on` d `, subject to automatic enrolment:` `auto-enrolled` `, has a guardian:` `has a guardian` `, has an Oranga Tamariki guardian:` `Oranga Tamariki guardian` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p's `already a member of a KiwiSaver scheme` OR `auto-enrolled` OR NOT `the Act applies to` p
            THEN `may not opt in`
        IF age AT LEAST 18 THEN `the person alone`
        IF age AT LEAST 16 AND (`has a guardian` OR `Oranga Tamariki guardian`) THEN `the person jointly with a guardian`
        IF age AT LEAST 16 THEN `the person alone, having no guardian`
        IF `Oranga Tamariki guardian` THEN `an Oranga Tamariki guardian in the person's name`
        OTHERWISE `a guardian in the person's name`
    WHERE
        age MEANS `the age of someone born` (p's `date of birth`) `on` d

§§ `Information, allocation and transfers (ss 42, 51, 56, 57)`

-- s 42(1)(a) the information pack "within 7 days of the employee starting the
-- new employment".
@ref s 42(1)(a)
GIVEN started IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give the information pack, employment started` started MEANS
    `the day` 7 `days after` started

-- s 51 allocation to a default scheme completes "62 days after the date on
-- which the Commissioner receives that notice"; s 75 contributions stay in
-- the holding account for "the 62-day period".
@ref ss 51, 75
GIVEN received IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day allocation completes, notice received` received MEANS
    `the day` 62 `days after` received
